{%- comment -%}
  Thumbnail for a navigation link.

  Every item in the shilo-2026-main menu is a real COLLECTION link with a
  resourceId, so link.object resolves to the collection and link.object.image is
  the department artwork the store already maintains. A plain URL item would give
  type == 'http_link' and no object, which is why the type is checked rather than
  the url: an http link to /collections/x looks identical in the menu but has no
  resource behind it, and reading .object.image off it would silently render nothing.

  FALLBACK (owner request: every menu entry shows a relevant image): when the
  collection has no image of its own, a product photo from that collection is
  used. The product is picked at offset `position` (the item's index within its
  sibling group) modulo the collection's product count — deterministic, and it
  keeps two sibling collections that share the same FIRST product (verified in
  this catalogue: ניקוי כללי / ניקוי רצפות both lead with the same VILEDA dolly)
  from rendering the same photo twice in one panel, because different rows sit
  at different offsets. The .products access only happens for collections with
  no image (14 of ~110 menu entries), so the per-render cost is bounded. The
  real fix — uploading images to those collections — is listed in
  docs/STORE-HEALTH.md; once an image exists it wins automatically.

  Only a width is requested. Asking for width AND height would make Shopify crop
  server-side, and these images are a mix of designed square tiles, product shots
  and brand wordmarks - cropping a wordmark to a square destroys it. The CSS box is
  fixed on both axes with object-fit: contain, so there is no layout shift and no
  need for width/height attributes here.

  Accepts:
    link     - a linklist link (required)
    size     - rendered CSS px, default 40. The request is 2x for retina.
    position - the link's index within its sibling group (forloop.index0);
               seeds the product-photo fallback. Default 0.
    class    - extra class on the img
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign nav_thumb_size = size | default: 40
  assign nav_thumb_2x = nav_thumb_size | times: 2
  assign nav_thumb_image = blank
  if link.type == 'collection_link' and link.object != blank
    assign nav_thumb_image = link.object.image
    if nav_thumb_image == blank and link.object.products_count > 0
      assign nav_thumb_pos = position | default: 0
      assign nav_thumb_pidx = nav_thumb_pos | modulo: link.object.products.size
      assign nav_thumb_image = link.object.products[nav_thumb_pidx].featured_image
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if nav_thumb_image != blank -%}
  <img
    class="nav-thumb{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
    style="--nav-thumb-size: {{ nav_thumb_size }}px"
    src="{{ nav_thumb_image | image_url: width: nav_thumb_2x }}"
    alt=""
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
  >
{%- endif -%}
